---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy | CookMushroom" description="How CookMushroom handles analytics data, advertising cookies, server logs, and messages sent to the site.">
  <main id="content" class="guide">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective November 1, 2026</p>
    <article class="prose">
      <p>CookMushroom is a public cooking reference. You can read the site without creating an account or submitting personal information.</p>
      <section>
        <h2>Information collected</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> the site measures page views and basic interactions. Google Analytics may collect device and browser details, approximate location, referring pages, and cookie or similar identifiers.</li>
          <li><strong>Server and security logs:</strong> our hosting and security provider, Cloudflare, may process IP addresses, request details, and security signals needed to deliver and protect the site.</li>
          <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> the site shows ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its advertising partners may use cookies or similar identifiers to show ads based on your visits to this and other sites, and to measure them. You can turn off personalised ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>. Google describes its use of this data in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. Visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked for consent before personalised ads are shown.</li>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> if you contact us, we receive the address and information you include in your message.</li>
          <li><strong>Affiliate links:</strong> some pages may link to products on Amazon. If you follow one, Amazon may set cookies to credit the referral and handles that data under its own privacy notice. CookMushroom does not receive your name, payment details or order contents. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>How information is used</h2>
        <p>We use this information to operate and secure the site, understand which cooking guides are useful, improve site content, and reply to questions or corrections.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>CookMushroom uses Cloudflare for hosting and security, Google Analytics for traffic measurement, and Google AdSense for advertising. Those providers process data under their own privacy terms. CookMushroom does not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser, use content-blocking tools, or use Google’s Analytics opt-out tools. Blocking analytics does not prevent access to CookMushroom.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Retention and requests</h2>
        <p>Analytics and security data are retained according to the settings and policies of the services above. To ask about a message you sent or request its deletion, email <a href="mailto:hello@cookmushroom.com">hello@cookmushroom.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>Material changes will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>